ae2/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": false, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "sing key.\n- `app/config.py` (lines 9\u201310) loads `settings.json` unchanged, so it doesn't catch the typo either.\n\n**Suggested fix:**\n1. In `settings.json`, rename `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"`. This alone makes `main.py` print `Total: 5.0`.\n2. Optionally, remove the `except KeyError: rate = 0` fallback in `main.py`, so a missing key fails with an error. `billing/report.py` already does this with `SystemExit`.\n\n`billing/report.py` and `billing/export/csv_writer.py` also read `fee_rate`. `main.py` doesn't import them, but they would fail on the same typo.\n\nDo you want me to apply the fix?\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nI renamed the `\"rat\"` key to `\"fee_rate\"` in `settings.json` line 2. All three paths that read the setting now work.\n\n**Files that read `fee_rate`:**\n\n| File | Line | How it reads it |\n|---|---|---|\n| `main.py` | 11 | `cfg[\"fee_rate\"]`, with a `KeyError` fallback to 0 |\n| `billing/report.py` | 7 | `get_setting(\"fee_rate\")`, which exits if the value is `None` |\n| `billing/export/csv_writer.py` | 8 | `settings.get(\"fee_\" + \"rate\")`, which exits if the value is `None` |\n\n`csv_writer.py` builds the key by concatenating two strings, so a plain search for `fee_rate` doesn't find it.\n\nOther places mention the name but don't read the setting:\n- `billing/invoice.py:5` uses `\"fee_rate\"` as a label string only.\n- `billing/discount.py:5` has a local variable called `archived_fee_rate` with a hardcoded 0.15.\n- `billing/audit.py` and `billing/tax.py` mention settings only in docstrings that say they are unrelated.\n\n**Results:**\n\n| Command | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `python3 main.py` | `Total: 0` | `Total: 5.0` |\n| `python3 -m billing.report` | `fee_rate is missing` | `Report fee: 0.5` |\n| `python3 -m billing.export.csv_writer` | `fee_rate is missing` | `CSV fee: 0.5` |\n\nI left the `except KeyError: rate = 0` fallback in `main.py` alone. It is what hid the typo, so say if you want it removed so a missing key fails loudly.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 5, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 158200, "requests_cache_write": 42605, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1661625, "requests_count": 16, "requests_input_uncached": 1505, "requests_output": 4082, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-subagent-followup:claude-opus-5-5:trial12", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 104, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-17T02:37:13.655456+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 2, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 36.132, "t_checker_s": 0.224, "t_env_setup_s": 0.004, "task": "trig-subagent-followup", "task_calls": 1, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 5587, "tokens_cache_read": 158200, "tokens_cache_write": 42605, "tokens_fresh": 2507, "tokens_input_uncached": 1505, "tokens_main_cache_read": 126739, "tokens_main_cache_write": 30783, "tokens_main_calls": 9, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 22, "tokens_main_output": 2485, "tokens_output": 4082, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 158200, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 42605, "tokens_proxy_calls": 16, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 1505, "tokens_proxy_output": 4082, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchain": {"ai": "5.0.8", "anthropic": "2.0.0", "bun"